# play — fail
#
# The play verb attempted and missed: the checks pass, the dice do not, the outcome block reports
# FAILURE, and nothing is learned. A failure costs one entry of the play's own table (the skipping
# stones: the thread lost, or a strained shoulder); which one is drawn, so it is not asserted here.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Shore" --period dawn --observe-only "Test Pebbles"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy fail-dice
goal play
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
regions

click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

expect FAILURE
expect-verb play
# The failure assertion that means something: the play's lesson did NOT land.
expect-no-state skills ducks_and_drakes
quit
